inline_comments.body:
@andyxning The point of this PR is to stop exact fp32 upcasts, the common case of a bf16/fp16 checkpoint loaded into an fp32 parameter, from printing one line per affected layer at every start; for hybrid Qwen3.x A_log that is one line per linear-attention layer. Two ways to keep the rest visible:

1. bf16/fp16 → fp32 at DEBUG for any model, every other mismatch (fp64 targets included) at WARNING.
2. Keep those at WARNING, but once per dtype pair instead of once per layer. Either works for me.
